  "assumptions": [
    "Copilot-to-agent integration is proposed; supported deployment mechanism must be verified.",
    "MCP client is an SDK role inside the host, not necessarily a separately deployed service.",
    "MCP gateway is a logical role that APIM can implement. This option separates MCP routing from downstream REST policy; it does not mandate buying two gateways.",
    "Control-plane edges describe configuration and token acquisition, not a live Entra call on every request.",
    "Never pass through inbound tokens to an unintended audience; acquire appropriately scoped downstream credentials.",
    "Edition, region, capacity, recovery and availability remain unspecified. No SLA is asserted.",
    "Tool calls need bounded timeouts and safe retry/idempotency design. Tool permissions and audit redaction require implementation and testing."
  ],
